# KS-987 — Wednesday's task for Ornith, item 1 only, **DOCUMENTATION (`Blockchain/Dev/deployment/DEPLOYMENT-ARCHITECTURE.md`, no code)** (written 2026-09-16 21:2x from the file at develop M55 `48e65c435`: `deployment/DEPLOYMENT-ARCHITECTURE.md` read whole (186 lines), the `**Redeploy runbook** (until scripted):` block at `:63-73` and the `Ops notes:` list at `:75-156` read in full; `docker-compose.yml` read for the api-gateway service's `volumes:` at `:553`. Pre-measured in a scratch clone at `48e65c435`: the insertion below applied with `git apply`, both Required tokens absent → present inside the section.)

## What to change (one paragraph)

The demo redeploy runbook (`:63-73`) rsyncs `Blockchain/Dev` to the VM and then runs
`docker compose build <changed services> && docker compose up -d`. It never restarts `api-gateway`.
The published OpenAPI spec `docs/openapi/secuura-api.yaml` reaches the gateway as a single-FILE bind
mount (`docker-compose.yml:553`, `:ro`). On the 2026-09-08 deploy (KS-987) that combination left the
gateway serving the OLD spec after rsync had written the new one, with every signal an operator checks
reading fine, until `docker compose restart api-gateway` was run. KS-987 item 1 asks for the restart
as a REQUIRED runbook step, with the mechanism written beside it so it is not dropped as cargo-cult.
This task adds ONE paragraph directly under the runbook's code block. Nothing existing changes. Items
2-4 of the ticket (project-notes wording, a post-deploy md5 assertion, a sweep of other file mounts)
are NOT this task.

