## The exact change — ONE INSERT-ONLY hunk, 10 new lines

Insert AFTER line 73 (the closing code fence of the redeploy runbook block, three backticks alone on
the line) and BEFORE line 74 (a blank line; line 75 is `Ops notes:`). The fence below holds ONLY the
added lines, each with a leading `+`. The FIRST added line is BLANK (a `+` and nothing else). The
context the hunk needs is copied VERBATIM from `files[...]`, never retyped from this brief: lines 71-73
above the insertion and lines 74-76 below it. Copy every `+` line character for character, including
every backtick; no `+` line contains a dollar sign, a backslash or an em dash.

```
+
+**Then restart the gateway, every time: `sudo docker compose restart api-gateway` (KS-987).**
+The published spec `docs/openapi/secuura-api.yaml` reaches `api-gateway` as a single-FILE bind
+mount (`docker-compose.yml`, read-only), and rsync replaces a changed file by writing a temp file
+and renaming it over the old one, which gives the new spec a new inode. On the 2026-09-08 deploy
+the file on the VM disk was the new spec while the copy inside the running gateway was still the
+old one, and `GET /api/docs/openapi.yaml` served the old bytes; rsync, the file on disk and the
+health check all looked right. Only `restart api-gateway` made the container, and the served spec,
+match the host. Restart it on every redeploy that changes the spec, including when `api-gateway`
+was not in the rebuilt set.
```

Do NOT touch lines 63-73 or 74-156; do NOT re-flow any existing line; do not add a second blank line.

## Required (the checker's proof — each token ABSENT in the section before, PRESENT after)
